<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  SignageMadeEasy kiosk labwc config — installed by provision.sh to
  ~/.config/labwc/rc.xml (the signage user's labwc config, not the system-wide
  /etc/xdg/labwc/rc.xml default).

  This exists for exactly one reason: labwc's HideCursor action, which cage (the
  compositor this replaced) never had any working equivalent for after five
  separate real-hardware-tested attempts — see signage-kiosk.service. There's no
  "hide the cursor automatically on startup" config in labwc itself, so the
  documented pattern (see labwc's own GitHub discussion #3190, "Automatically
  hide cursor and fullscreen app on startup in Labwc") is to bind it to a
  keybind and fire that keybind synthetically once at startup. F13 is used
  because it's a key that doesn't exist on any real keyboard likely to be
  attached to this kiosk device, so nothing else can ever trigger it by
  accident. ~/.config/labwc/autostart fires it via `ydotool key 183:1 183:0`
  (183 is F13's raw Linux input event keycode, KEY_F13 in input-event-codes.h —
  ydotool takes raw keycodes, not key names).

  WarpCursor is stacked with HideCursor per labwc's own docs: "Use together
  with the WarpCursor action to not just hide the cursor but to additionally
  move it away to prevent e.g. hover effects." Moving it doesn't matter much
  here (this kiosk has no real pointer device — confirmed via `lsusb` showing
  nothing attached — so nothing will make the cursor reappear per labwc's own
  caveat that it "becomes visible again on following pointer/stylus/touchpad
  actions"), but it's free to include.

  UNVERIFIED: HideCursor was added in labwc 0.8.4. The exact labwc version
  Raspberry Pi OS Trixie/armhf ships has not been confirmed from this sandbox
  (this repo could only install/inspect labwc 0.7.1 on Ubuntu, which predates
  HideCursor entirely). If the installed labwc is older, this action is
  silently unknown to it and the cursor stays visible — XCURSOR_SIZE=0 in
  signage-kiosk.service is the fallback for exactly that case.
-->
<labwc_config>
  <keyboard>
    <keybind key="F13">
      <action name="HideCursor" />
      <action name="WarpCursor" to="output" x="center" y="center" />
    </keybind>
  </keyboard>
  <!-- Chromium runs kiosk-mode fullscreen (its own fullscreen request) as the
       only app this device ever runs — no server-drawn title bar/borders
       should ever be visible, but this closes the gap for whatever brief
       moment exists before Chromium's fullscreen request takes effect. -->
  <windowRules>
    <windowRule identifier="*" serverDecoration="no" />
  </windowRules>
</labwc_config>
